Describe your networking experience. How do you go about troubleshooting complex networks ?
On the system and virtualization level, I do have experience and good analysis skills at the network level, to understand which layer an issue is coming from, including other network protocols like DHCP, link aggregation, and simple routing.

For example, if I had an issue where two servers can’t communicate with each other, I start my analysis by going through all the layers — from physical, to VLAN, to IP configuration, to talking to the gateway, traceroute, checking ports, checking app level like HTTP headers or the protocol used…

But everything beyond that — like complex routing (EIGRP or OSPF) or advanced network setups like SD-WAN — I understand the basics and fundamentals, but the network experts are the ones who handle it. So sometimes I can fix the issue myself, and sometimes it requires help from one of our network colleagues.

